
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>CSS Box Model</title>

<style>
body {
font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
background-color: #f0f4f8;
text-align: center;
padding: 20px;
}

h1 {
color: darkblue;
}

.box {
width: 250px;
padding: 30px;
border: 5px solid blue;
margin: 30px auto;
background-color: lightblue;
}

p {
color: black;
}
</style>
</head>

<body>

<h1>CSS Box Model</h1>

<p>The CSS Box Model has four parts:</p>

<div class="box">
<h2>Content</h2>
<p>This is the content inside the box.</p>
</div>

<h2>Four Parts of the Box Model</h2>

<p><strong>Content:</strong> The information inside the box.</p>
<p><strong>Padding:</strong> Space around the content.</p>
<p><strong>Border:</strong> The line around the padding.</p>
<p><strong>Margin:</strong> Space outside the border.</p>

</body>
</html>
